    "extraction_notes": [
      "Target identity retained exactly from job metadata: 2N7002KX, Shenzhen JingYang, n-channel MOSFET. The supplied PDF header displays JYELECTRONICS.",
      "The supplied PDF SHA-256 is 5985b9de76d57552adbdcfe239bea8d824b67653f30f7883855cabc43c1b9bf7.",
      "The supplied PDF contains five pages: maximum ratings and package marking on p. 1, tabulated electrical characteristics on p. 2, typical output and transfer characteristics on p. 3, typical gate-charge, diode, thermal, safe-operating-area, and capacitance plots on p. 4, and package dimensions on p. 5.",
      "RDS(ON) table rows preserve both typical and inclusive maximum values: 2 ohm typical and 3 ohm maximum at VGS = 10 V and ID = 0.3 A, and 2.1 ohm typical and 3.5 ohm maximum at VGS = 5 V and ID = 0.3 A.",
      "The capacitance table publishes Ciss = 21 pF typical, Coss = 11 pF typical, and Crss = 4 pF typical at VDS = 25 V, VGS = 0 V, and f = 1.0 MHz. Values are converted to farads; the corresponding maximum values are not substituted into the scalar typical fields.",
      "Curve points are compact direct readings from the supplied typical output, transfer, and capacitance plots on p. 3 and p. 4. No points were generated by interpolation between source values. The transfer and capacitance plots retain their printed test conditions and axis scales."
